The video backends are built as separate shared objects from one source file
each (add_library(moonlight-aml SHARED ./src/video/aml.c)), but they call
helpers that live in the executable - aml.c uses ensure_buf_size() from
src/util.c. Nothing exports those, so .dynsym holds none of them and loading
the backend dies at the first call:

  ./moonlight: symbol lookup error: libmoonlight-aml.so:
      undefined symbol: ensure_buf_size

ENABLE_EXPORTS puts the executable's symbols in its dynamic table, which is
what a plugin dlopen'd against its host needs. Affects every backend built
this way, not just aml.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@
 add_subdirectory(libgamestream)
 
 add_executable(moonlight ${SRC_LIST})
+set_target_properties(moonlight PROPERTIES ENABLE_EXPORTS ON)
 target_link_libraries(moonlight m)
 target_link_libraries(moonlight gamestream)
 
